6	Blindfold of the Unseen	The sown image of eyes on this blindfold are often attributed to "the unseen" and are frequently used to depict ghosts, spirits specters and other unseen creatures.\n\nInvisibility: When this blindfold completely covers a wearers eyes they become invisible. Anything the wearer is carrying or wearing is also invisible as long as it is on their person. If the wearer makes an attack or casts a spell the Invisibility ends. If the blindfold is removed the invisibility is likewise ended. While invisible the wearer is able to perceive creatures hidden by invisibility or similar spells as though they are glowing spectral beings.	3	\N	\N	Magic	\N
7	Hot and Bothered	This golden pistol is inscribed with alluring silhouettes  and flames. When loaded it produces a faint moaning sound and when fired, the shot is transformed into a blast of flame. This gun uses your charisma modifier for attack and damage rolls dealing 2d10 (+charisma) fire damage on a hit. The shooter of this pistol also takes 1d4 force damage from the gun's massive recoil. After being fired once it must be reloaded which required 1 full action\n	3	\N	\N	Weapon	\N
8	Devil's Armor	Medium armor (cursed item, armor)\nAC: 18 (no addition from dex)\nCategory: Items\nItem Rarity: Very Rare\nModifiers: Ac +1\nStealth: Disadvantage\nWeight: 45\n\n"This Black and Gold armor may look imposing but is surprisingly lightweight and maneuverable. The Clerical Leader of the True Descendants Tarin Dardendrian wore it into battle as a way to intimidate his foes, tearing his victims to shreds with his hands. some say the armor was a gift from a dark being and slowly drove him mad."\n\n<div>While wearing this armor, you gain a <i>+1 bonus to AC</i>, and you can understand and speak Infernal. In addition, the armor's clawed gauntlets turn unarmed strikes with your hands into magic Weapons that deal 1d8 slashing damage, with a <i>+1 bonus to attack and damage</i> rolls.</div>\n<div><b>Legacy of Tarin Daardendrian</b>. Your predecessor grants you some of his commanding presence and charm. While wearing this armor you may choose to add 1d6 to any charisma ability check or saving throw. Doing so saps a bit of your own life force, you also take the amount added in necrotic damage.</div>\n<div><b>Curse</b>: Once you don this Cursed armor, you can't doff it unless you are targeted by the remove curse spell or similar magic. While wearing the armor, you have disadvantage on Attack rolls targeting Devils and on saving throws against being charmed or otherwise mentally manipulated. When the curse breaks, or if you die, the armor lets out a blast of necrotic energy causing every creature within <i>30 feet</i> to make a <i>DC 15 constitution saving throw</i>, on a fail they take <i>4d6 necrotic damage</i>, on a success they take half as much damage. </div>	3	\N	\N	Clothing	63
9	Charm of Good Fortune	<div>With the favor of this charm any pure-hearted venture is sure to succeed</div>	25	\N	\N	Magic	\N
