COPY public."Location" (id, title, is_sub, parent_location_id, project_id, description, type, image_id) FROM stdin;
31	Skirr	t	16	3	"As you approach the isle of Skirr, you see a thick blanket of clouds swirling around its peaks, creating an otherworldly aura. Suddenly, the clouds part, revealing a breathtaking sight. Below, you see a vibrant world of floating mountains and cascading waterfalls. The sky dwarves of Skirr flit between the jagged cliffs, their lithe forms darting through the air like lightning bolts. You can feel the rush of wind and excitement as they race through the slipstream wind-tunnels, their shouts of joy echoing across the valleys. Skirr is a land of wonder and danger, a place where the laws of physics seem to have been suspended. The isle is dotted with soaring peaks and valleys, some of which are suspended high above the clouds. Waterfalls tumble down from these heights, forming glittering streams and pools that sparkle in the sunlight. The landscape is dotted with exotic flora and fauna, some of which have adapted to the unique gravitational conditions of the isle.\nThe sky dwarves of Skirr are the undisputed masters of this land, their aerial prowess honed by generations of living in the clouds. They have built their homes and fortresses among the peaks, using their agility and strength to scale the sheer rock faces. The isle is dotted with slipstream wind-tunnels, which the sky dwarves use to travel between the crags at breakneck speeds.\nBut Skirr is not without its dangers. The isle is constantly buffeted by storms and strong winds, and one misstep could send even the most skilled sky dwarf plummeting to their death. As a result, the isle has a rugged, wild feel to it, with danger lurking around every corner. But for those who can master the skies, Skirr is a land of limitless potential, where anything is possible.\n"	\N	\N
