1	Haversnippets	f	\N	2	Sed nec nibh porta, venenatis nulla in, facilisis odio. Etiam et tempus tellus. Donec et est commodo, sollicitudin tortor quis, laoreet nisl. Phasellus maximus dolor diam, sit amet vehicula ipsum tristique at. Suspendisse id risus lacus. Aenean ultrices libero purus, id malesuada lorem elementum sit amet. Vestibulum rhoncus, massa non feugiat tristique, enim est accumsan libero, quis cursus sapien nisl et est. Ut efficitur nisl sit amet tellus efficitur placerat. Proin ultricies, ante quis sollicitudin sollicitudin, turpis nibh tristique metus, ut auctor augue sem et massa. Sed tortor odio, euismod vitae convallis a, rutrum et metus.	Planet	\N
11	A Breath of Bloodhaven	t	9	3	A Small cafe owned by Patricio themed after bloodhaven. They serve tea and information. On birthdays a large pink octopus made of paper mache drops from the ceiling 	\N	\N
5	Testland	t	4	8	Yeah well it's a place 	Region	\N
7	Greyfall City	t	16	3	As your ship breaks through the final clouds, the breathtaking sight of Greyfall City unfolds before you. The sprawling metropolis is built upon a massive island, with buildings and structures jutting out at every angle, cascading down the sides of the landmass. The city streets are a hive of activity as ships, carts, caravans, and people bustling about their lives, creating a chaotic yet mesmerizing scene.\n     Above it all towers a tall mountain, right at the heart of the city, its peak crowned with a magnificent twisting spire overlooking the entire metropolis. \n     The city is surrounded by a sea of spiraling lights, marking hundreds of ships that follow trade routes in and out of Greyfall. Some so large it's hard to tell if they're ships at all or smaller orbiting islands. As you approach, you can't help but feel a sense of awe and wonder at the grandeur and beauty of Greyfall City.\n	Continent	6
6	Test Town	t	5	8	Yeah it's a test town it sucks 	Town	\N
8	Iron District	t	7	3	 A multi-level metropolis and home to some of the most premier Dragonmarked houses. The iron districts are the central hustle-and-bustle location in Greyfall.	City	\N
9	Rustworth	t	7	3	Intricate networks of bridges, trollies, and trains wind through the "City of Invention" where brilliant minds experiment with the latest technologies. The architecture reflects this spirit of innovation, with buildings featuring radically different designs from floor to floor as new owners add their own unique perspectives. Massive gears loom above the walkways, some power huge machines, others provide transportation for people and goods, and still others serve purposes beyond comprehension, possibly aesthetic. The residents of Rustworth may be gruff, but they warmly welcome outsiders, particularly tourists with coins to spend as they explore the city's unique atmosphere.\n	City	\N
10	Sul Outpost	t	9	3	A location in south rustworth Owned by the Sul Family. Complex undercity machinery allow many secret exits and entrances from below 	\N	\N
12	Badbelow	t	7	3	A dark and gothic region. Due to the rotation of the island, badbellow rarely gets more than a few hours of direct sunlight in a day. The city is known for its spectacular stone and marble architecture, gargoyles line streets illuminated by rows of pale green lanterns. Most folk tend to want to avoid badbellow, but it's denizens couldn't dream of leaving, many being from a variety of species that detest sunlight.\n	\N	\N
15	Talons Point	t	7	3	The Arcane Academy! Ages past a small moon orbiting greyfall was split by a scientist's arcane experiments gone awry. However before the chunks could crash into the fledgling city it was bound together and locked into place as a permanent fixture. Now, between the two halves stands the beautiful Talon's Point Academy. Greyfall may be known for its technology, but this refuge is home to a host of arcane and druidic masters and students who work tirelessly to refine their craft. No greater wizards are known to exist, outside the Empire	\N	\N
14	The Citadel	t	7	3	 A beautiful twisting spire rises high above Greyfall. It serves as the hub of political power and for the Hygar Republic, where the great and the good gather to discuss matters of state. The Citadel is not only a symbol of the city's grandeur and prosperity, but it also represents the hope and aspirations of its people for a better and peaceful future. The shining central spire is a beacon of guidance for all who call Greyfall home, standing as a testament to the strength and resilience of her people.	City	\N
13	Fort Faith	t	7	3	The Military might of Greyfall is fort faith. Here the greatest paladins and clerics are trained to wield divine magic to support the brave men at arms, the inquisitive detectives and the Noble Sky Dwarves trained here to operate as police and security throughout and around the city.	City	\N
21	Bloodhaven	t	16	3	“The Auburn Isle'' is suspended in a never-ending autumn. Most vegetation is constantly dying off except for a particular pink leafed tree and a forest of giant pines on the south  end. The island has retained its independence largely because nobody wants it and is home to all manner of scallywags and rogues. Bloodhaven is known for bad service, bad weather, bad people and really bad ale.\n	Continent	11
16	Wyrld	f	\N	3	They say chunks of existence were once scooped from their places in the multiverse and suspended here in perpetual orbit around Jotun. Collectively this place is known as Wyrld.\nThe intense atmospheric conditions of the massive Jotun prevents life, or even approach, but the surrounding chunks maintain their own miniature atmospheres and gravities. The lowlands are warm and some even so hot as to be unlivable, the Highlands, conversely, become colder and colder the further you ascend. Above it all is the Ice cloud, a massive arctic waste where evaporated water rising through the atmosphere has frozen instantly on approach, as it gets weighted down the lowest ice begins to melt and rain. \nThe people of Wyrld are fascinated by the vast open expenses between floating islands. Airships of various forms and construction exploring the sky in search of riches, adventure and freedom. Pirates roam the skies ready to swoop down on unsuspecting merchant ships. Large slow carriers powered by heated air and balloons carry hundreds of refugees toward a new life in Greyfall city. Giant eagles or even Wyvern are harnessed to imperial warships pulling them gracefully through the clouds.\nOutWyrlders, people from other planes, have been known to find their way into Wyrld by various means. Some via failed plane-shifting experiments, others are banished by the gods, and a few are portaled aboard Ghost Ships. These self-piloting mechanical flying vessels wander the skies until a crew of OutWyrlders are deposited on their decks.They then navigate themselves to the nearest settlement and self-decommission.	Planet	7
18	Pierdawn	t	17	3		\N	\N
19	Capiël	t	17	3	The capital of Silean. Capiel is a lovely, if simple city with a fair skyport overhead, wedged between two large mountain peaks. The people here are kind but mostly focused on business	\N	9
20	St Garous Abbey	t	17	3	High in the mountains sits the monastery of st. Garou. Most know the monks to be worshipers of the moon goddess and guardians of ancient magical secrets. However, few realize the monastery is also a safe haven for lycanthropes who seek to control their curse, or must be contained when control is lost. Tragedy befell the Monastary, leaving few survivors. But the land was quickly restored and the ruins now are teeming with life as though blessed by the moon Goddess herself	\N	10
22	Haven City	t	21	3	The best of the worst '', Haven City is falling apart at the seams. As the central hub in Booldhaven, and with little official oversight, Haven city is a great place for those who don't want to be found. Local gangs run the show and have recently worked to organize the city's defenses against threats. The recent occupation of the Iman Empire and exploitation by the Far Reach Co. was ended by mysterious means. The future looks bright for Haven city for the first time in memory as plants have been seen growing and rumors of giant protectors begin to spread."\n	\N	\N
24	Burrow’s Bay 	t	21	3	A small mining community. Mostly Halflings. Swirling winds in the bay make it difficult to navigate 	\N	\N
25	Frementine	t	21	3	A vineyard town. Known for making large quantities of terrible wine	\N	\N
26	Lyfell	t	21	3	A failed colony established long ago in the great forests, Tall trees that poison the earth and prevent other things from growing. Lyfell was destroyed, left in ruins and mostly forgotten.	\N	\N
28	Ima Ektu	t	16	3	is a scorching desert wasteland, where the sun beats down mercilessly upon the sands, baking them to a brilliant golden hue. Amidst the rolling dunes and jagged rocks, nomadic tribes of barbarians roam free, salvaging remnants of fallen skyships which crashed due to the intense heat to form weapons and armor.\nDespite the desolate appearance of the desert, there are still pockets of life to be found on Ima Ektu. The heat and sand have shaped the land into a maze of towering stone formations and sharp shale cliffs, creating a unique and captivating landscape that is equal parts beautiful and deadly. But Ima Ektu was not always this way. Once, it was home to the Sun Elves, a proud and noble people who lived in harmony with the land. However, their peaceful existence was shattered when the Iman Empire came to conquer and claim the island as their own. In a fierce battle, the Sun Elves were defeated and eradicated, their memory fading into the sands of time.\nDespite its harsh conditions, Ima Ektu is a land of stunning beauty, from the sun-bleached dunes to the mysterious pyramids that loom in the distance. A land of contrasts, where life is a struggle, but where the rugged people who call it home are forged into something greater.\n	Continent	\N
27	Ima Theylmar	t	16	3	The floating island of Ima Theylmar is a primeval land of unparalleled beauty and mystery. A place where ancient stone pillars soar high above the clouds and enormous canyons carve deep into the earth, leaving in their wake a stunning tapestry of natural wonders. Endless waterfalls cascade over the cliffs, fed by the deep springs that run the length of the island, creating a bed of mist and steam in the skies below. This rugged, prehistoric landscape is teeming with life, from massive dinosaurs to exotic flora and fauna.\nIma Theylmar is the heart of the Iman Empire, a society that values magic above all else and shuns advancing technology. The Leonins, the imperial ruling class, hold sway over the entire land. The beauty and raw power of the island are paralyzing. Everything here is ancient, beautiful, and intimidating. The sheer size of the creatures that roam this land is enough to make even the bravest adventurer think twice about venturing into the unknown \n	Continent	\N
29	Wyr's Deep	t	16	3	Wyrsdeep is renowned for its abundant natural resources that are so highly sought after that the land was eventually stripped away in the pursuit of material and riches. Now only a massive floating ocean remains in its place, suspended in the skies of Wyrld and constantly battered by storms. Despite the turbulence, the central submerged landmass serves as a hub for underwater people and mining operations, with a rich and diverse underwater ecosystem thriving beneath the waves. The floating ocean is a proud member of Hygar, a republic of floating lands in the upper atmosphere of Wyrld, and the inhabitants of Wyrdeep have adapted and built a thriving underwater civilization. Many mysteries lie beneath the waves for even the native Wyrs do not dare dive so deep as to discover them all.\n	\N	\N
30	FaeWood	t	17	3	“A wild wood warps the wit, of weary wonders within. Meandering makes for meddled minds. Tarrying tends to truncate time. The fae are few but friendly folk, but strangers still scare them so.”\n	\N	\N
32	Elvandarreef	t	16	3	Ever changing, ever gliding, drifting about the vastness of Wyrld's skies, an outpouring of clouds and water anchor one small magical city in place. An age-old forgotten rumor, a creation story lulling younglings to sleep,  tells of an old alchemist. He was enchanted by the possibilities of the sky and the grace of flowing waters, dedicating his life to harnessing the two. Decades into research and study, the alchemist found himself in the possession of a rather rare artifact: a Decanter of Endless Water, a silly thing, if you did not know it's true magic. His decanter’s origin story changes with every telling, fluid as the waves he was so enraptured by. Gifted to him by a Celestial lover, or found deep within the heart of Jotun itself, it matters not. The relic itself is considered sacred,  the seed of Elvanderreef.\nCuriosity turned the Alchemist reckless and hasty in his experimentation. The decanter exploded. If we are to believe the rather romantic notion of the Celestial lover, she would have descended upon the alchemist, shielding him. The arcane blast and the divine protection collided, creating a rift, a tear between the sea and sky. Still to this day, water pours endlessly through the rift, creating steam vents and clouds, dizzyingly swirling, eventually to be sucked back in. Wondrous in stories, the reality of this phenomenon causes an erratic orbital trajectory, making Elvandarreef impossible to chart, only to be found by accident or magical means. Local residents are a small population of moon elves. A good-natured people with no political inclinations,  they have little to no involvement in the disputes of Hygar and the Empire. Under the protection of the gentle Moon Goddess Aruna, they want for nothing their own island doesn't provide and rarely find the call to leave.\nWayward travelers do occasionally happen upon Elvandarreef, despite its elusive nature. Visitors are an oddity, especially to curious moon elf children. Met with nothing but kindness, they are encouraged to enjoy the breathtaking views, fish-based cuisines and local customs. Perhaps most thrilling and dangerous of all are dives into the magical waves below the city. A vast ocean is held within a pocket dimension beneath the surface, filled with all manner of aquatic life and mysteries. Strange creatures sometimes find their way out of the depths disturbing the balance. Traveling adventurers often take it upon themselves to face the ancient aquatic threats. Those who manage to return boast mighty treasures, ancient riches and tales of wonder from beneath Elvanderreef.\n	Area	\N
