34	Albion's Rest	t	8	3	<div>As you approach the small municipality at the Bottom of the Iron Districts, the first thing that catches your eye is the sprawling ranch filled with magnificent horses, their glistening coats shimmering in the sunlight. The air is thick with the earthy scent of hay and the gentle whinnies of the horses, making it clear that this is a town that takes pride in its equestrian heritage.\nAs you venture into the community, the legacy of the Ancient hero Albion Blackstar becomes apparent in the intricate murals and statues that dot the streets. It's clear that his heroism is a source of great inspiration for the people here, and their cultural memory is intertwined with the legend of the brave warrior.\nAs you continue your exploration, you come across a strange astral elf who has made his home in the town. He exudes an otherworldly aura that is both alluring and unsettling, and his presence seems to have added a layer of intrigue to this already fascinating place.\n\nIn the north side of town, a small community of homeless folks has set up camp, creating a stark contrast to the otherwise orderly and well-kept streets. Despite their circumstances, the people here seem to be filled with a sense of camaraderie and unity that is heartwarming to witness.\n\nAnd then there's the Far Reach Co, whose lift is a marvel of engineering, silently transporting goods up to the upper city with ease. The company's presence is a reminder of the complex political and economic web that underpins this town, but it's also a testament to the ingenuity and resourcefulness of the people who call it home.\nBut perhaps the most intriguing feature of this place is the wishing well that seems to possess a mysterious magic. The waters shimmer with an ethereal light, and those who toss a coin into the well swear that their wishes have been granted, no matter how impossible they may seem.\n\nAll in all, this town is a captivating hodgepodge of oddities, where the fantastical meets the mundane, and the past meets the present. It's a place where anything is possible, and where adventure awaits at every turn.\n\n</div>	Village	16
17	Silean	t	16	3	<div>A smaller island, briming with magic. Silean is home to a massive fae-wood and a small range of mountains inhabited by wearwolves.</div><span id="docs-internal-guid-bf124dde-7fff-16bd-7978-1ebfb2b220ba"><br></span>	Continent	8
