4	4	Prankster, mischievous, joker, enjoys good banter, sarcastic	Not tied down, free to roam, find rare items and treasure\n	Not well connected to physical reality, gets lost in though, hearing voices. Tied to the ethereal psychic realm\n	Does not keep a stable or reliable position in life, not to be fully trusted in any field or practice.\n	His heart torn by a bloody family history, Van disowned his blood lineage in exchange for the road. He no longer wanted to belong to the toxic cult he was born into in the lower realms, but rather find his way amongst the highland cities beyond the threshold, amongst more civil and common folk. He became a hardened thief, mostly against the wealthy lords of the feudal lands, stealing enough to be comfortable and keep a low profile. He has even managed to play the roles of nobleman and gained access to their castle treasuries. It was fairly unusual to see a Tiefling in the city, but not unheard of, as many have abandoned the old daemon way to seek a new life. Van finds utility and mystery wherever he goes, always exploring into the depths and behind closed doors. His path lead him to the boat which took him across to the land of Wyrld, where he begins his adventure.	35	5' 10"	140	Red	Gray	White	is currently a woman\nhooded cloak\npsi-replenish is out till next full rest	Haunted one	Chaotic Neutral	Generally disheveled and delirious, tattered and worn but quality linen and jean clothing, various cuffs and rings, longish hair, short beard, short horns. dark gray purplish skin tone. Young but weathered. Casual and relaxed with a bit of crazed-confidence. Easy to underestimate but just dangerous enough not to become too involved with. Easy for for other crazy people to find a friend in.	Allied with the dragon house family Hanselton of Grayfall City. 
14	14	\N	\N	\N	\N	Batholomeow is a Cathian, a member of high society for the Nami Empire. He had inherited an estate from an abusive father and was forced into a marriage and made to have a family. Wanting to escape the stifling life of a noble, Bartholomeow had dreams of being a world-famous pirate. \n\nSo instead of being content with his life of privilege, he had used his wealth to hire a crew, leave his family and sail the open the skies. One problem, he was not experienced or equipped to navigate turbulent weather. So a storm had blown his ship off course where him and his crew got lost. He was unable to reunite with his crew, surviving in the wilds on his own. \n\nBartholomeow no longer sought the adventure he did when he was a lad of mind. He has an overwhelming sense of fear and self-preservation, motivated by that more than any inclination to seek out danger. He knows he can't return home to his family, ashamed for abandoning a child. 	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Nami Empire
